From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: security changes seen on this phone and tracker
 signals on the App security page

App security & privacy (Settings > Apps) now answers two things it
marked unknown:

* Changes seen on this phone: the page keeps, per app and user and in
  device-protected storage, the last snapshot it saw (version, target SDK,
  signing certificates, requested permissions, exported components with
  no guarding permission, elevated services, tracker signals) and lists
  what changed at the next look, classed Info, Privacy signal, Review,
  Elevated or Critical with no score. The first look only stores a
  baseline. Only apps whose page was opened have a record, so it reads
  "since this phone first looked". Nothing leaves the phone.
* Tracker libraries: a small local signature list (TrackerSignatures,
  list 2026-10) matched against manifest component class names and the
  META-INF/*.version files in the APKs. INFERRED: a signal from names,
  not proof that the code ran; no match does not prove there is none.

Pure models SecuritySnapshot, SecurityChanges, SecurityLedger and
TrackerSignatures with host tests (SecurityHistoryTest). Changes only
files created by 0601 and 0604.

---
